,"identifier":"NP_001259004.1","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/protein/NP_001259004.1","className":"DatabaseIdentifier","schemaClass":"DatabaseIdentifier"}],"referenceDatabase":{"@id":"28","dbId":2,"displayName":"UniProt","accessUrl":"http://purl.uniprot.org/uniprot/###ID###","name":["UniProt","SWALL","SPTR","SwissProt","SPTREMBL"],"url":"http://www.uniprot.org","resourceIdentifier":"MIR:00100164","identifiersPrefix":"uniprot","className":"ReferenceDatabase","schemaClass":"ReferenceDatabase"},"physicalEntity":[{"@id":"29","dbId":3222218,"displayName":"USP10 [nucleoplasm]","stId":"R-HSA-3222218","stIdVersion":"R-HSA-3222218.1","maxDepth":1,"name":["USP10","Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 10","Deubiquitinating enzyme 10","Ubiquitin thioesterase 10","Ubiquitin-specific-processing protease 10","KIAA0190"],"speciesName":"Homo sapiens","species":{"@id":"30","dbId":48887,"displayName":"Homo sapiens","name":["Homo sapiens","H. sapiens","Hs","human","man"],"taxId":"9606","crossReference":[{"@id":"31","dbId":72938,"displayName":"NCBI_taxonomy:9606","databaseName":"NCBI Taxonomy","identifier":"9606","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Taxonomy/Browser/wwwtax.cgi?mode=Info&id=9606","className":"DatabaseIdentifier","schemaClass":"DatabaseIdentifier"}],"abbreviation":"HSA","className":"Species","schemaClass":"Species"},"endCoordinate":798,"referenceType":"ReferenceGeneProduct","startCoordinate":2,"referenceEntity":{"@ref":"1"},"className":"Protein","inDisease":false,"schemaClass":"EntityWithAccessionedSequence"},{"@id":"32","dbId":6782986,"displayName":"K63polyUb-USP10 [cytosol]","stId":"R-HSA-6782986","stIdVersion":"R-HSA-6782986.2","maxDepth":1,"name":["K63polyUb-USP10","USP10","Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 10","Deubiquitinating enzyme 10","Ubiquitin thioesterase 10","Ubiquitin-specific-processing protease 10","KIAA0190"],"speciesName":"Homo sapiens","species":{"@ref":"30"},"endCoordinate":798,"referenceType":"ReferenceGeneProduct","startCoordinate":2,"referenceEntity":{"@ref":"1"},"className":"Protein","inDisease":false,"schemaClass":"EntityWithAccessionedSequence"},{"@id":"33","dbId":6782974,"displayName":"USP10 [cytosol]","stId":"R-HSA-6782974","stIdVersion":"R-HSA-6782974.2","maxDepth":1,"name":["USP10","Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 10","Deubiquitinating enzyme 10","Ubiquitin thioesterase 10","Ubiquitin-specific-processing protease 10","KIAA0190"],"speciesName":"Homo sapiens","species":{"@ref":"30"},"endCoordinate":798,"referenceType":"ReferenceGeneProduct","startCoordinate":2,"referenceEntity":{"@ref":"1"},"className":"Protein","inDisease":false,"schemaClass":"EntityWithAccessionedSequence"}],"checksum":"E6BA77E2B5CE2B3F","comment":["FUNCTION Hydrolase that can remove conjugated ubiquitin from target proteins such as p53/TP53, RPS2/us5, RPS3/us3, RPS10/eS10, BECN1, SNX3 and CFTR (PubMed:11439350, PubMed:18632802, PubMed:31981475). Acts as an essential regulator of p53/TP53 stability: in unstressed cells, specifically deubiquitinates p53/TP53 in the cytoplasm, leading to counteract MDM2 action and stabilize p53/TP53 (PubMed:20096447). Following DNA damage, translocates to the nucleus and deubiquitinates p53/TP53, leading to regulate the p53/TP53-dependent DNA damage response (PubMed:20096447). Component of a regulatory loop that controls autophagy and p53/TP53 levels: mediates deubiquitination of BECN1, a key regulator of autophagy, leading to stabilize the PIK3C3/VPS34-containing complexes (PubMed:21962518). In turn, PIK3C3/VPS34-containing complexes regulate USP10 stability, suggesting the existence of a regulatory system by which PIK3C3/VPS34-containing complexes regulate p53/TP53 protein levels via USP10 and USP13 (PubMed:21962518). Does not deubiquitinate MDM2 (PubMed:20096447). Plays a key role in 40S ribosome subunit recycling when a ribosome has stalled during translation: acts both by inhibiting formation of stress granules, which store stalled translation pre-initiation complexes, and mediating deubiquitination of 40S ribosome subunits (PubMed:27022092, PubMed:31981475, PubMed:34348161, PubMed:34469731). Acts as a negative regulator of stress granules formation by lowering G3BP1 and G3BP2 valence, thereby preventing G3BP1 and G3BP2 ability to undergo liquid-liquid phase separation (LLPS) and assembly of stress granules (PubMed:11439350, PubMed:27022092, PubMed:32302570). Promotes 40S ribosome subunit recycling following ribosome dissociation in response to ribosome stalling by mediating deubiquitination of 40S ribosomal proteins RPS2/us5, RPS3/us3 and RPS10/eS10, thereby preventing their degradation by the proteasome (PubMed:31981475, PubMed:34348161, PubMed:34469731). Part of a ribosome quality control that takes place when ribosomes have stalled during translation initiation (iRQC): USP10 acts by removing monoubiquitination of RPS2/us5 and RPS3/us3, promoting 40S ribosomal subunit recycling (PubMed:34469731). Deubiquitinates CFTR in early endosomes, enhancing its endocytic recycling (PubMed:19398555). Involved in a TANK-dependent negative feedback response to attenuate NF-kappa-B activation via deubiquitinating IKBKG or TRAF6 in response to interleukin-1-beta (IL1B) stimulation or upon DNA damage (PubMed:25861989). Deubiquitinates TBX21 leading to its stabilization (PubMed:24845384). Plays a negative role in the RLR signaling pathway upon RNA virus infection by blocking the RIGI-mediated MAVS activation. Mechanistically, removes the unanchored 'Lys-63'-linked polyubiquitin chains of MAVS to inhibit its aggregation, essential for its activation (PubMed:37582970).CATALYTIC ACTIVITY Thiol-dependent hydrolysis of ester, thioester, amide, peptide and isopeptide bonds formed by the C-terminal Gly of ubiquitin (a 76-residue protein attached to proteins as an intracellular targeting signal).ACTIVITY REGULATION Specifically inhibited by spautin-1 (specific and potent autophagy inhibitor-1), a derivative of MBCQ that binds to USP10 and inhibits deubiquitinase activity. Regulated by PIK3C3/VPS34-containing complexes.SUBUNIT Found in a deubiquitination complex with TANK, USP10 and ZC3H12A; this complex inhibits genotoxic stress- or interleukin-1-beta (IL1B)-mediated NF-kappa-B activation by promoting IKBKG or TRAF6 deubiquitination (PubMed:25861989). Interacts with IKBKG; this interaction increases in response to DNA damage (PubMed:25861989). Interacts with TANK; this interaction increases in response to DNA damage (PubMed:25861989). Interacts with TRAF6; this interaction increases in response to DNA damage (PubMed:25861989). Interacts with ZC3H12A; this interaction increases in response to DNA damage (PubMed:25861989). Interacts with G3BP1 (via NTF2 domain) and G3BP2 (via NTF2 domain); inhibiting stress granule formation (PubMed:11439350, PubMed:23279204, PubMed:27022092, PubMed:31981475, PubMed:32302570, PubMed:36183834, PubMed:36279435).INTERACTION Cytoplasmic in normal conditions (PubMed:20096447). After DNA damage, translocates to the nucleus following phosphorylation by ATM (PubMed:20096447).ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS Widely expressed.INDUCTION Following DNA damage. Down-regulated in renal cell carcinomas.PTM Phosphorylated by ATM following DNA damage, leading to stabilization and translocation it to the nucleus.PTM Ubiquitinated. Deubiquitinated by USP13.SIMILARITY Belongs to the peptidase C19 family. USP10 subfamily."],"description":["recommendedName: fullName evidence=\"27\"Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 10 ecNumber evidence=\"10 11 17 20\"3.4.19.12 alternativeName: Deubiquitinating enzyme 10 alternativeName: Ubiquitin thioesterase 10 alternativeName: Ubiquitin-specific-processing protease 10"],"geneName":["USP10","KIAA0190"],"isSequenceChanged":false,"keyword":["3D-structure","Acetylation","Alternative splicing","Autophagy","Cytoplasm","DNA damage","DNA repair","Endosome","Hydrolase","Nucleus","Phosphoprotein","Protease","Proteomics identification","Reference proteome","Thiol protease","Ubl conjugation","Ubl conjugation pathway"],"secondaryIdentifier":["UBP10_HUMAN","B2RDJ8","B4DS84","Q9BWG7","Q9NSL7"],"sequenceLength":798,"species":{"@ref":"30"},"chain":["initiator methionine:1","chain:2-798"],"referenceGene":[{"@id":"34","dbId":8989892,"displayName":"ENSEMBL:ENSG00000103194 USP10","stId":"ensembl:ENSG00000103194","databaseName":"ENSEMBL","identifier":"ENSG00000103194","url":"https://www.ensembl.org/id/ENSG00000103194","moleculeType":"Entity","geneName":["USP10","KIAA0190"],"species":{"@ref":"30"},"className":"ReferenceDNASequence","schemaClass":"ReferenceDNASequence"},{"@id":"35","dbId":12783591,"displayName":"UCSC:Q14694 USP10","databaseName":"UCSC","identifier":"Q14694","url":"https://genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgLinkIn?id=Q14694&resource=uniprot","moleculeType":"Entity","geneName":["USP10","KIAA0190"],"className":"ReferenceDNASequence","schemaClass":"ReferenceDNASequence"},{"@id":"36","dbId":11397291,"displayName":"BioGPS Gene:9100 USP10","databaseName":"BioGPS Gene","identifier":"9100","url":"https://biogps.org/gene/9100","moleculeType":"Entity","geneName":["USP10","KIAA0190"],"className":"ReferenceDNASequence","schemaClass":"ReferenceDNASequence"},{"@id":"37","dbId":11412948,"displayName":"COSMIC (genes):USP10 USP10","databaseName":"COSMIC (genes)","identifier":"USP10","url":"https://cancer.sanger.ac.uk/cosmic/gene/overview?ln=USP10","moleculeType":"Entity","geneName":["USP10","KIAA0190"],"className":"ReferenceDNASequence","schemaClass":"ReferenceDNASequence"},{"@id":"38","dbId":11432759,"displayName":"CTD Gene:9100 USP10","databaseName":"CTD Gene","identifier":"9100","url":"https://ctdbase.org/detail.go?type=gene&acc=9100","moleculeType":"Entity","geneName":["USP10","KIAA0190"],"className":"ReferenceDNASequence","schemaClass":"ReferenceDNASequence"},{"@id":"39","dbId":11450823,"displayName":"dbSNP Gene:9100 USP10","databaseName":"dbSNP Gene","identifier":"9100","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/snp/9100","moleculeType":"Entity","geneName":["USP10","KIAA0190"],"className":